      "problem": "$\\frac{{a}^{5}}{{a}^{9}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We subtract the exponents, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}^{5}}{{a}^{9}} & = \\\\ {a}^{(5-9)} & = \\\\ {a}^{-4} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we convert the negative exponent to a positive exponent by taking the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{-4} & =\\frac{1}{{a}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}^{5}}{{a}^{9}}=\\frac{1}{{a}^{4}}.\n$$",
